    text: `O glorious Saint Anthony, wonder worker and patron of lost things, I come to you today in my necessity. Just as you recovered the lost manuscript of Saint Thomas Aquinas and restored the lost silver chalice to its rightful owner, so I implore you to intercede before God for the recovery of what I have lost. Whether it be a material possession, a lost opportunity, or the loss of spiritual graces, I trust in your powerful intercession. Saint Anthony, you who are so near to the heart of God, obtain for me what is truly good for my soul. If it be God's holy will, return to me what I have lost; and if not, grant me the peace to accept His providential designs with a contented heart. Amen.`
